Welcome to Hollywood.
欢迎来到好莱坞。

970
00:39:53.960 --> 00:39:55.740
Should we go to Nashua?
我们要去纳舒厄吗？

971
00:39:55.740 --> 00:40:00.160
We do, because Pam has talked Michael into giving his presentation.
我们要去，因为帕姆说服了迈克尔去进行他的演讲。

972
00:40:00.380 --> 00:40:05.780
Because then maybe they'll all talk about how great Michael was and Holly will hear about it, right?
因为这样也许他们都会谈论迈克尔有多棒，然后霍莉就会听说了，对吧？

973
00:40:05.940 --> 00:40:08.580
That's the way you show AJ, right?
这就是你向AJ示威的方式，对吧？

974
00:40:09.000 --> 00:40:09.580
Yes.
是的。

975
00:40:09.940 --> 00:40:10.680
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

976
00:40:10.800 --> 00:40:12.760
At the beginning, it's going great.
一开始，一切都很顺利。

977
00:40:13.200 --> 00:40:14.120
It is.
确实如此。

978
00:40:14.260 --> 00:40:15.840
He's doing a fantastic job.
他表现得非常出色。

979
00:40:15.980 --> 00:40:17.960
Just listen to all of his movie references.
听听他所有的电影引用就知道了。

980
00:40:20.340 --> 00:40:23.500
Good morning, Vietnashua.
早安，越南舒厄。

981
00:40:23.500 --> 00:40:27.100
Ah, sales.
啊，销售。

982
00:40:27.560 --> 00:40:31.580
Sales is what brings us together today.
销售是今天把我们聚在一起的原因。

983
00:40:33.180 --> 00:40:45.060
How do we deal with clients who say, frankly, my dear, I don't give a damn about paper, and get them to show us the money?
我们该如何应对那些说“坦白说，亲爱的，我一点也不在乎纸张”的客户，并让他们把钱掏出来呢？

984
00:40:45.700 --> 00:40:48.440
Well, we are going to find out today.
好吧，我们今天就要找出答案。

985
00:40:49.200 --> 00:40:50.720
I had written this down.
我把这个写下来了。

986
00:40:50.720 --> 00:41:00.240
It's so interesting that you played that clip, because I wondered, do our younger viewers get all of the references in Michael's opening remarks?
你播放那段剪辑很有意思，因为我在想，我们年轻的观众能听懂迈克尔开场白里的所有梗吗？

987
00:41:00.420 --> 00:41:01.800
Do they know these movies?
他们知道这些电影吗？

988
00:41:02.080 --> 00:41:06.980
Good Morning Vietnam, Princess Bride, Gone with the Wind, and Jerry Maguire.
《早安越南》、《公主新娘》、《乱世佳人》和《甜心先生》。

989
00:41:07.240 --> 00:41:10.020
I guess this is Michael's taste in movies.
我想这就是迈克尔的电影品味。

990
00:41:10.220 --> 00:41:10.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

991
00:41:10.860 --> 00:41:12.620
But do people know all those today?
但现在的人都知道这些电影吗？

992
00:41:13.080 --> 00:41:16.040
I mean, you've got to know Princess Bride, right?
我是说，你总得知道《公主新娘》吧，对吧？

993
00:41:16.280 --> 00:41:16.960
I think.
我想是吧。

994
00:41:17.660 --> 00:41:18.840
I don't know.
我不知道。

995
00:41:18.840 --> 00:41:20.600
Oh, I don't know.
噢，我不知道。

996
00:41:21.180 --> 00:41:22.440
But he's got them.
但他确实用上了。

997
00:41:22.560 --> 00:41:23.200
They're laughing.
他们在笑。

998
00:41:23.360 --> 00:41:26.400
They love his, like, voices he's doing.
他们很喜欢他模仿的那些声音。

999
00:41:26.920 --> 00:41:28.340
Nashua likes Michael.
纳舒厄喜欢迈克尔。

1000
00:41:28.340 --> 00:41:33.380
From the receptionist to his opening remarks, they're eating out of the palm of his hand.
从前台接待到他的开场白，他们都被他迷住了。

1001
00:41:33.380 --> 00:41:40.700
If only he could get over this Holly thing, he would finally have a day where he was the king of comedy like he's always wanted.
如果他能放下霍莉这件事，他终于能过上一天他梦寐以求的喜剧之王的生活了。

1002
00:41:40.940 --> 00:41:46.860
Those 30 seconds you just heard are the best that it is, because that's how quickly it falls apart.
你们刚才听到的那30秒就是全场最佳，因为一切崩塌得就是这么快。

1003
00:41:46.860 --> 00:41:50.380
Because Michael zeroes in on AJ.
因为迈克尔盯上了AJ。

1004
00:41:50.660 --> 00:41:51.520
He can't help it.
他控制不住自己。

1005
00:41:52.380 --> 00:41:52.860
Salesmen.
推销员们。

1006
00:41:54.120 --> 00:41:54.600
Salespeople.
销售人员们。

1007
00:41:55.280 --> 00:41:57.560
He's going to pick a random salesperson.
他要随便挑一个销售人员。

1008
00:41:57.660 --> 00:41:58.360
You there, sir.
那位先生。

1009
00:41:58.500 --> 00:41:58.840
You.
就是你。

1010
00:41:59.160 --> 00:41:59.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1011
00:42:00.180 --> 00:42:01.640
What's it like to be you?
成为你是什么感觉？

1012
00:42:01.880 --> 00:42:03.260
Oh, here we go.
噢，开始了。

1013
00:42:03.400 --> 00:42:03.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1014
00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:06.880
And then Michael has a full-on panic attack.
然后迈克尔就彻底恐慌发作了。

1015
00:42:07.080 --> 00:42:10.340
He winds up on the ground, and he crawls out of the room.
他瘫倒在地，然后爬出了房间。

1016
00:42:10.440 --> 00:42:10.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1017
00:42:11.100 --> 00:42:12.300
Leaving Pam.
留下了帕姆。

1018
00:42:12.980 --> 00:42:13.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1019
00:42:14.260 --> 00:42:20.080
Well, before we get to what Pam is going to do, I wanted to shout out a few crew cameos.
好吧，在讲帕姆要做什么之前，我想提一下几位客串的工作人员。

1020
00:42:20.620 --> 00:42:21.300
Oh, okay.
噢，好的。

1021
00:42:21.780 --> 00:42:29.840
So, sitting next to AJ, the woman who asked the question about discounts from distributors, that was Mary Wall.
坐在AJ旁边，那个问关于经销商折扣问题的女士，是玛丽·沃尔。

1022
00:42:30.220 --> 00:42:30.600
Yes.
是的。

1023
00:42:30.600 --> 00:42:36.060
And she was a member of our production staff, and she is delightful and wonderful.
她是我们的制作人员之一，她非常可爱，也非常棒。

1024
00:42:36.600 --> 00:42:39.780
She has gone on to become a producer and a director.
她后来成为了一名制片人和导演。

1025
00:42:40.100 --> 00:42:43.640
She currently is working on a documentary called The Fan Connection.
她目前正在制作一部名为《粉丝连接》的纪录片。

1026
00:42:43.820 --> 00:42:47.640
You can actually check it out at fanconnectionmovie.com.
你们可以去fanconnectionmovie.com看看。

1027
00:42:47.640 --> 00:42:48.500
You can see a trailer.
可以看到预告片。

1028
00:42:48.720 --> 00:42:51.780
It's all about the hockey fans in Buffalo.
讲的是布法罗的冰球粉丝。

1029
00:42:52.140 --> 00:42:53.380
Oh, I would love that.
噢，我一定会喜欢的。

1030
00:42:53.380 --> 00:42:55.120
And their commitment to their hockey team.
以及他们对冰球队的忠诚。

1031
00:42:55.120 --> 00:42:56.260
And you know I love hockey.
你知道我喜欢冰球的。

1032
00:42:56.500 --> 00:42:58.420
So, anyway, check out the trailer, guys.
总之，大家去看看预告片吧。

1033
00:42:58.420 --> 00:42:59.980
I love sports documentaries.
我喜欢体育纪录片。

1034
00:43:00.300 --> 00:43:00.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1035
00:43:00.740 --> 00:43:01.260
Love them.
非常喜欢。

1036
00:43:01.500 --> 00:43:09.820
And then, sitting in the row in front of AJ with the red hair, was Claire Scanlon, our editor.
然后，坐在AJ前排那个红头发的，是我们的剪辑师克莱尔·斯坎伦。

1037
00:43:10.180 --> 00:43:12.060
And Pam's going to call her Freckles.
帕姆会叫她“雀斑”。

1038
00:43:12.300 --> 00:43:16.980
Claire is a full-on badass, amazing editor, and now prolific director.
克莱尔是个彻头彻尾的狠角色，了不起的剪辑师，现在也是多产的导演。

1039
00:43:17.180 --> 00:43:17.500
Yes.
是的。

1040
00:43:17.680 --> 00:43:21.800
And then I have another guest star I want to mention, Michael McCartney.
然后我还有另一位客串明星想提一下，迈克尔·麦卡特尼。

1041
00:43:21.800 --> 00:43:29.640
He played the other Nashua employee who says, what does this have to do with sales, when Michael is disintegrating?
他扮演了另一个纳舒厄的员工，当迈克尔崩溃时，他说“这和销售有什么关系”。

1042
00:43:30.060 --> 00:43:32.140
He has a very extensive resume.
他的履历非常丰富。

1043
00:43:32.560 --> 00:43:36.620
He is the producer and director of the series The Millionaires on Amazon Prime.
他是亚马逊Prime剧集《百万富翁》的制片人和导演。

1044
00:43:36.620 --> 00:43:38.320
But here's what I want to tell you.
但我有件事想告诉你们。

1045
00:43:38.500 --> 00:43:38.720
What?
什么？

1046
00:43:38.720 --> 00:43:40.480
This is the first time I've seen this.
这是我第一次看到这个。

1047
00:43:40.580 --> 00:43:46.120
And all of my Googling of all of our guest stars, well, now I don't know what to expect.
我谷歌了所有客串明星，现在我不知道该期待什么了。

1048
00:43:46.940 --> 00:43:50.640
Michael McCartney has been on Law & Order.
迈克尔·麦卡特尼上过《法律与秩序》。

1049
00:43:50.900 --> 00:43:51.280
Okay.
好的。

1050
00:43:51.560 --> 00:43:52.960
Law & Order SVU.
《法律与秩序：特殊受害者》。

1051
00:43:53.120 --> 00:43:53.640
Oh, well.
好吧。

1052
00:43:54.080 --> 00:43:58.400
And Law & Order Criminal Intent, The Trifecta.
还有《法律与秩序：犯罪倾向》，这可是“三连冠”啊。

1053
00:43:58.720 --> 00:43:59.640
Holy cow!
天哪！

1054
00:43:59.940 --> 00:44:00.480
All three.
三部全齐了。

1055
00:44:01.180 --> 00:44:02.100
Not on Monk.
《神探阿蒙》里没有。

1056
00:44:02.420 --> 00:44:03.360
Not on Monk.
《神探阿蒙》里没有。

1057
00:44:03.760 --> 00:44:04.840
There's still room.
还有机会。

1058
00:44:05.020 --> 00:44:05.620
There's still room.
还有机会。

1059
00:44:05.760 --> 00:44:11.100
Future guest star, if you could be on all three Law & Orders and Monk, I'm going to drive to your house and give you a cake.
未来的客串明星们，如果你们能同时上这三部《法律与秩序》和《神探阿蒙》，我就开车去你家给你送个蛋糕。

1060
00:44:12.900 --> 00:44:21.060
So, when I was trading emails with Rob, I was like, Rob, you've got to share what it was like in that room when Steve, as Michael, is falling apart.
所以，当我和罗伯互通邮件时，我说，罗伯，你一定要分享一下，当史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔在会议室里崩溃时，现场是什么样的。

1061
00:44:21.400 --> 00:44:21.720
Yes.
没错。

1062
00:44:22.240 --> 00:44:23.440
And singling you out.
而且还专门针对你。

1063
00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:25.000
I mean, I don't know.
我是说，我不知道。

1064
00:44:25.100 --> 00:44:25.800
How did you do that?
你是怎么做到的？

1065
00:44:25.860 --> 00:44:26.780
How did you get through it?
你是怎么熬过来的？

1066
00:44:26.900 --> 00:44:27.900
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的回答。

1067
00:44:27.900 --> 00:44:43.740
My memories of shooting that scene in the conference room with Steve are mostly about just trying not to laugh because sometimes I just start laughing when people are funny because,
关于在会议室拍那场戏，我对史蒂夫的记忆大多是关于努力忍住不笑，因为有时候当别人很有趣时，我就会忍不住笑出来，因为，

1068
00:44:44.080 --> 00:44:52.780
really, I feel like a lot of times on comedy shows, you're trying to make the other person laugh.
说真的，我觉得在喜剧节目里，很多时候你都在试图逗笑对方。

1069
00:44:52.940 --> 00:44:56.560
In a way, you're kind of trying to f*** with them a little bit.
某种程度上，你其实是在试图捉弄他们一下。

1070
00:44:56.560 --> 00:45:05.700
But so, anyway, I was just trying to keep a straight face because Steve is so funny and Jenna is so funny and everybody on the show is so funny.
但总之，我当时只是努力保持严肃，因为史蒂夫太搞笑了，珍娜也太搞笑了，剧组里的每个人都太搞笑了。

1071
00:45:05.820 --> 00:45:07.120
And I also get very nervous.
而且我也非常紧张。

1072
00:45:07.280 --> 00:45:14.880
I get nervous going into a new show and, you know, there's this whole other culture there already established.
我进入一个新剧组时会感到紧张，你知道，那里已经形成了一套完全不同的文化。

1073
00:45:14.880 --> 00:45:20.120
When you're a guest actor on a show, it's different because you don't know what you're walking into.
当你作为客串演员去演一部剧时，感觉是不一样的，因为你不知道自己将要面对什么。

1074
00:45:20.120 --> 00:45:24.800
So, I was a little bit nervous and Steve is just, you know, iconic.
所以，我当时有点紧张，而且史蒂夫，你知道，他是偶像级的。

1075
00:45:25.080 --> 00:45:26.240
Steve is just so funny.
史蒂夫真是太搞笑了。

1076
00:45:26.480 --> 00:45:36.980
And when he's kind of coming at me like that, he's, you know, putting me down and ignoring me and calling me names in a very funny way.
当他那样冲着我来的时候，他，你知道，在贬低我、无视我，还用一种非常搞笑的方式骂我。

1077
00:45:36.980 --> 00:45:39.900
But it's all so funny.
但这真的太搞笑了。

1078
00:45:39.980 --> 00:45:42.140
So, mostly trying not to laugh.
所以，我大部分时间都在努力忍住不笑。

1079
00:45:43.180 --> 00:45:47.620
I loved his description of what it's like to be a guest actor on a show.
我很喜欢他对于作为客串演员去演一部剧的描述。

1080
00:45:48.160 --> 00:45:55.180
Walking into the world and it's a comedy and it's supposed to be funny, but then you're not supposed to laugh.
走进那个世界，那是一部喜剧，本该很有趣，但你却不能笑。

1081
00:45:55.180 --> 00:45:57.980
I just, I related to all of that so much.
我真的，我对此感同身受。

1082
00:45:58.140 --> 00:45:58.700
I did too.
我也是。

1083
00:45:58.960 --> 00:46:04.220
Well, we also asked him, does he still get recognized as AJ?
好吧，我们还问了他，他现在还会因为AJ这个角色被认出来吗？

1084
00:46:04.760 --> 00:46:07.700
He's been on, what did you say, 140?
他演过，你刚才说多少部？140部？

1085
00:46:08.060 --> 00:46:10.720
140 movies and TV shows.
140部电影和电视剧。

1086
00:46:11.160 --> 00:46:12.740
Does he get recognized as AJ?
他还会因为AJ被认出来吗？

1087
00:46:13.040 --> 00:46:14.040
Let's find out.
我们来看看。

1088
00:46:14.680 --> 00:46:18.660
Do I get recognized as AJ from The Office?
我会因为《办公室》里的AJ被认出来吗？

1089
00:46:18.660 --> 00:46:20.460
Are you kidding me?
你在开玩笑吗？

1090
00:46:20.700 --> 00:46:21.200
Yes.
会。

1091
00:46:22.460 --> 00:46:23.800
Yes, a lot.
会，经常被认出来。

1092
00:46:24.020 --> 00:46:26.040
And I'm so thankful for it.
对此我非常感激。

1093
00:46:26.140 --> 00:46:29.100
It is very fun to be recognized.
被认出来是一件很有趣的事。

1094
00:46:29.100 --> 00:46:34.540
No matter what people tell you, it is fun because it's, you know, it's people love it.
不管别人怎么说，这确实很有趣，因为，你知道，大家都很喜欢这个角色。

1095
00:46:34.680 --> 00:46:38.180
They love the show and that's fun.
他们热爱这部剧，这很有意思。

1096
00:46:38.480 --> 00:46:44.480
You know, like everyone had an opinion about Michael and Holly's relationship and I was just standing in the way.
你知道，每个人对迈克尔和霍莉的关系都有自己的看法，而我当时正好挡在中间。

1097
00:46:44.480 --> 00:46:46.400
So, I would get threatened by strangers.
所以，我还会受到陌生人的威胁。

1098
00:46:46.840 --> 00:46:48.500
You know, it was crazy.
你知道，那真是太疯狂了。

1099
00:46:48.820 --> 00:46:51.740
In fact, people used to come up to me out of the blue.
事实上，人们过去常常会冷不丁地走过来找我。

1100
00:46:51.740 --> 00:46:59.240
I remember people would sometimes whisper in my ear, like come up behind me and say, you stay away from Holly.
我记得有人有时会凑到我耳边低语，比如从背后走过来对我说，离霍莉远点。

1101
00:46:59.440 --> 00:47:00.920
You stay away from Holly.
离霍莉远点。

1102
00:47:01.340 --> 00:47:05.780
And what's crazy is that my wife in real life, her name is Holly.
最疯狂的是，我现实生活中的妻子也叫霍莉。

1103
00:47:06.220 --> 00:47:16.640
So, I would have to decide in about two seconds, okay, is this someone that used to date my wife in real life that I should murder?
所以我得在两秒钟内决定，好吧，这人是跟我现实中的妻子约会过，我该杀了他吗？

1104
00:47:17.380 --> 00:47:21.880
Or is this just a fan of The Office acting like a creeper?
还是说这只是个《办公室》的粉丝在装变态？

1105
00:47:22.880 --> 00:47:25.300
I love that his wife's name is Holly.
他妻子叫霍莉这一点太棒了。

1106
00:47:25.540 --> 00:47:26.200
I know!
我知道！

1107
00:47:26.400 --> 00:47:27.200
That's insane.
太疯狂了。

1108
00:47:27.440 --> 00:47:31.320
That is crazy, though, that people go up to him and they're like, leave Holly alone.
不过人们跑过去跟他说“离霍莉远点”确实很疯狂。

1109
00:47:31.500 --> 00:47:31.880
And he's like, wait, what?
然后他会说，等等，什么？

1110
00:47:31.880 --> 00:47:32.600
Get away from Holly.
离霍莉远点。

1111
00:47:32.640 --> 00:47:33.380
Wait, that's my wife.
等等，那是我老婆。

1112
00:47:33.480 --> 00:47:35.120
Oh, you're, oh, okay.
哦，你是，哦，好吧。

1113
00:47:35.280 --> 00:47:36.220
Oh, I know what you are.
哦，我知道你是谁了。

1114
00:47:36.540 --> 00:47:36.940
Amazing.
太神奇了。

1115
00:47:37.420 --> 00:47:40.020
Well, thank you, Rob, for sending in your audio clips.
好吧，谢谢你，罗布，发来你的音频片段。

