Lady, I thought you were doing a bit to be bad, right?
女士，我还以为你是故意演得那么烂，对吧？

1140
00:48:39.320 --> 00:48:39.780
Yes.
是的。

1141
00:48:39.780 --> 00:48:43.680
And that is what Mindy and Ken Kwapis thought on set.
明迪和肯·卡皮斯在片场也是这么想的。

1142
00:48:44.140 --> 00:48:46.860
They were crying laughing when I did it.
我表演的时候他们都笑哭了。

1143
00:48:47.220 --> 00:48:51.220
Mindy said it was genius that I was doing it so bad.
明迪说我演得那么烂简直是天才之举。

1144
00:48:51.380 --> 00:48:51.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1145
00:48:51.900 --> 00:48:56.920
And I was texting with her because I was like, Mindy, do you remember this episode?
我当时在给她发短信，我说，明迪，你还记得这一集吗？

1146
00:48:57.080 --> 00:49:00.420
And she said, yes, I thought you were so funny that day.
她说，记得，我觉得那天你太搞笑了。

1147
00:49:00.600 --> 00:49:01.820
You're Forrest Gump.
你是阿甘。

1148
00:49:01.820 --> 00:49:05.400
It was such a funny choice, you know, to be bad.
演得烂真是一个有趣的决定，你知道吗。

1149
00:49:06.180 --> 00:49:09.580
And I was like, Mindy, that was my literal best effort.
我说，明迪，那真的是我尽了全力了。

1150
00:49:10.900 --> 00:49:14.460
My acting limitations made me genius.
我的演技局限成就了我的天才。

1151
00:49:14.700 --> 00:49:22.600
Like, that's one of those things where, like, if I tried to be bad, it wouldn't have been as good as me giving it my best effort.
就像那种情况，如果我故意演得很烂，反而没法达到我全力以赴的效果。

1152
00:49:22.860 --> 00:49:24.340
I can't do it better than that.
我没法做得比那更好了。

1153
00:49:24.440 --> 00:49:25.300
I need to hear it.
我得听听看。

1154
00:49:25.380 --> 00:49:26.260
I need to hear it.
我得听听看。

1155
00:49:26.340 --> 00:49:27.180
I got to hear it.
我一定要听听看。

1156
00:49:27.240 --> 00:49:28.120
I got to hear it.
我一定要听听看。

1157
00:49:28.120 --> 00:49:29.020
I'm getting my lap.
我正准备去跑一圈。

1158
00:49:29.060 --> 00:49:29.920
I got to hear it.
我一定要听听看。

1159
00:49:30.220 --> 00:49:32.940
I got Nat with that information in my brain.
我脑子里装着那条信息，还告诉了Nat。

1160
00:49:32.940 --> 00:49:38.460
I've got to hear it because I thought, like Mindy, that you were doing a bit.
我必须得听听，因为我当时和Mindy一样，以为你在演戏。

1161
00:49:38.820 --> 00:49:39.300
No.
没有。

1162
00:49:39.680 --> 00:49:40.960
At, like, I'm going to read it.
我打算读出来。

1163
00:49:41.280 --> 00:49:43.260
My Forrest Gump kind of crappy.
我那蹩脚的阿甘正传模仿秀。

1164
00:49:43.600 --> 00:49:45.620
But no, it was your best effort, honey.
但不是的，亲爱的，那是你尽了全力的表现。

1165
00:49:45.760 --> 00:49:50.620
I listened to his voice in my head over and over and over and over again.
我在脑海里一遍又一遍、反反复复地听他的声音。

1166
00:49:50.620 --> 00:49:52.320
And I tried to mimic it perfectly.
我试着完美地模仿它。

1167
00:49:52.600 --> 00:49:54.140
I have never loved you more.
我从未像现在这样爱你。

1168
00:49:54.140 --> 00:49:58.820
Knowing now that that Forrest Gump was your earnest best effort.
知道那个阿甘正传的模仿是你真心实意的全力以赴。

1169
00:49:58.980 --> 00:49:59.400
It was.
确实是。

1170
00:50:00.940 --> 00:50:03.760
Sales is like a box of chocolates.
销售就像一盒巧克力。

1171
00:50:04.060 --> 00:50:07.320
You never know which vendor you're going to get.
你永远不知道你会遇到哪家供应商。

1172
00:50:09.460 --> 00:50:10.360
Forrest Gump.
阿甘正传。

1173
00:50:11.140 --> 00:50:11.820
Lady.
女士。

1174
00:50:12.160 --> 00:50:14.520
That's the cutest thing ever.
那真是太可爱了。

1175
00:50:14.840 --> 00:50:16.620
That is the cutest thing.
那真是最可爱的事了。

1176
00:50:16.880 --> 00:50:17.440
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1177
00:50:17.600 --> 00:50:19.200
Look at Devin and Cassie.
看Devin和Cassie。

1178
00:50:19.340 --> 00:50:21.180
They're cracking up.
他们笑得前仰后合。

1179
00:50:21.540 --> 00:50:23.380
You guys, is that adorable?
伙计们，那是不是很可爱？

1180
00:50:23.920 --> 00:50:24.540
Come on.
得了吧。

1181
00:50:25.100 --> 00:50:25.820
So cute.
太可爱了。

1182
00:50:25.960 --> 00:50:26.580
We love it.
我们很喜欢。

1183
00:50:27.300 --> 00:50:28.060
Thank you, guys.
谢谢你们。

1184
00:50:28.400 --> 00:50:29.100
Thank you.
谢谢。

1185
00:50:29.660 --> 00:50:31.220
I loved doing that scene.
我很喜欢拍那场戏。

1186
00:50:31.220 --> 00:50:32.960
I loved the chainsaw.
我喜欢那把电锯。

1187
00:50:33.240 --> 00:50:34.100
I loved the chainsaw.
我喜欢那把电锯。

1188
00:50:34.120 --> 00:50:39.160
It was one of my most, you know, this was one of the few times when I was called upon
那是我最……你知道，这是我为数不多几次被要求

1189
00:50:39.160 --> 00:50:42.940
to do, like, what would you call it?
去做，怎么说呢？

1190
00:50:43.120 --> 00:50:44.340
Like, lead the group?
比如，带领团队？

1191
00:50:44.540 --> 00:50:46.240
To be the comedy protagoniSt.
成为喜剧主角。

1192
00:50:46.660 --> 00:50:46.820
Yes.
没错。

1193
00:50:46.820 --> 00:50:49.000
I was usually the receiver of comedy.
我通常是喜剧效果的接收者。

1194
00:50:49.000 --> 00:50:54.660
My job on this show was to amplify a comedic moment with my deadpan reaction.
我在这个节目里的工作就是用我面无表情的反应来放大喜剧时刻。

1195
00:50:55.180 --> 00:51:00.120
But in this case, I got to pitch the comedy ball, and it felt really good.
但在这种情况下，我成了抛出喜剧梗的人，感觉真的很棒。

1196
00:51:00.120 --> 00:51:02.460
Other people reacted off of you.
其他人根据你的表现做出反应。

1197
00:51:02.760 --> 00:51:03.020
Yes.
是的。

1198
00:51:03.260 --> 00:51:04.240
And it was fun.
那很有趣。

1199
00:51:04.500 --> 00:51:10.840
Well, one of my favorite things to watch play out in any movie or TV show is when a
嗯，在任何电影或电视剧中，我最喜欢看的情节之一就是当一个

1200
00:51:10.840 --> 00:51:14.640
character decides to step up to the plate and then bails.
角色决定挺身而出，结果却临阵脱逃。

1201
00:51:16.100 --> 00:51:22.720
So, at the end, when Pam got out the chainsaw and was like, cutting down the competition.
所以，最后帕姆拿出电锯，就像是在砍掉竞争对手一样。

1202
00:51:23.220 --> 00:51:23.420
Yeah.
没错。

1203
00:51:23.420 --> 00:51:24.920
The bail is my favorite.
保释那段我最喜欢。

1204
00:51:25.080 --> 00:51:26.140
She's like, I'm out.
她就像是说，我撤了。

1205
00:51:26.680 --> 00:51:29.500
Well, during all this, Michael has gone over to Holly's desk.
嗯，就在这期间，迈克尔走到了霍莉的办公桌前。

1206
00:51:30.560 --> 00:51:33.160
He's stroking her yellow cardigan.
他抚摸着她那件黄色开衫。

1207
00:51:33.340 --> 00:51:36.000
He cuts half of the sleeve off.
他剪掉了半个袖子。

1208
00:51:36.220 --> 00:51:36.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1209
00:51:37.060 --> 00:51:39.000
That made me laugh so hard, Jenna.
那段真的让我笑得不行，珍娜。

1210
00:51:39.580 --> 00:51:47.760
And then he, like, pushes the chair in, and this screensaver pops up of Martin Short,
然后他把椅子推回去，屏幕上弹出了马丁·肖特的屏保，

1211
00:51:47.980 --> 00:51:49.080
which is so perfect.
简直太完美了。

1212
00:51:49.280 --> 00:51:50.280
As Ed Grimley.
扮演艾德·格里姆利的那个。

1213
00:51:50.420 --> 00:51:50.960
Yes.
没错。

1214
00:51:51.460 --> 00:51:53.460
You know what Randy Cordray told me?
你知道兰迪·科德雷跟我说了什么吗？

1215
00:51:53.620 --> 00:51:53.860
What?
什么？

1216
00:51:54.300 --> 00:51:55.440
That little moment.
就那个小细节。

1217
00:51:56.120 --> 00:51:57.120
Like, that was the whole thing.
那可是整件事的重点。

1218
00:51:57.280 --> 00:52:00.040
He said, we had this graphic artist on staff.
他说，我们当时有个平面设计师在职。

1219
00:52:00.200 --> 00:52:01.320
His name was Michael Marcus.
他叫迈克尔·马库斯。

1220
00:52:01.520 --> 00:52:07.820
And he had to build that on-screen computer graphic where there were these documents on
他得制作那个电脑屏幕图形，上面有那些文档，

1221
00:52:07.820 --> 00:52:10.420
the homepage, that picture of Martin Short.
还有主页上那张马丁·肖特的照片。

1222
00:52:10.600 --> 00:52:15.200
They had to get permission to license that photo from Getty Images.
他们得从盖蒂图片社获得那张照片的授权许可。

1223
00:52:15.800 --> 00:52:20.500
I mean, that little moment, that was someone's day creating that.
我是说，就那个小细节，那是某人花了一整天做出来的。

1224
00:52:21.160 --> 00:52:23.820
I love watching the show and thinking of those details.
我喜欢看这部剧，并思考那些细节。

1225
00:52:24.460 --> 00:52:29.380
Well, to finish out the Nashua Branch storyline, Pam and Michael, they pack up.
好了，为了结束纳舒厄分公司的剧情线，帕姆和迈克尔收拾好东西离开了。

1226
00:52:29.500 --> 00:52:30.840
I love when Pam was like, don't look up.
我喜欢帕姆说“别抬头”的时候。

1227
00:52:30.940 --> 00:52:31.540
Don't look up.
别抬头。

1228
00:52:31.660 --> 00:52:33.400
Don't look up when they're packing up the car.
当他们在装车时，别抬头。

1229
00:52:33.400 --> 00:52:35.280
And they go to a diner.
然后他们去了一家餐馆。

1230
00:52:35.500 --> 00:52:42.760
And Michael confesses that, A, he cut off part of her sweater, and that he saw a dear Michael
迈克尔坦白说，第一，他剪掉了她毛衣的一部分，而且他看到了她桌面上一个“亲爱的迈克尔”

1231
00:52:42.760 --> 00:52:45.820
folder on her desktop, and he copied it.
文件夹，他还拷贝了一份。

1232
00:52:45.980 --> 00:52:46.920
He's got it.
他拿到了。

1233
00:52:47.620 --> 00:52:49.620
And Pam says, you can't read that.
帕姆说，你不能读那个。

1234
00:52:50.100 --> 00:52:51.360
But I can read it.
但我能读。

1235
00:52:52.040 --> 00:52:52.440
Right.
没错。

1236
00:52:52.540 --> 00:52:53.240
Pam can read it.
帕姆能读。

1237
00:52:53.320 --> 00:52:57.780
And I won't tell you what the specifics are, but I can tell you if she still likes you.
我不会告诉你具体内容，但我可以告诉你她是否还喜欢你。

1238
00:52:58.020 --> 00:53:00.040
We had a lot of fan mail about that.
我们收到了很多关于那段的粉丝来信。

1239
00:53:00.240 --> 00:53:02.620
Emma S., Eric M., and Zachary C.
艾玛·S、埃里克·M和扎卡里·C

1240
00:53:02.820 --> 00:53:05.340
all wanted to know, was there a letter?
都想知道，真的有一封信吗？

1241
00:53:05.720 --> 00:53:08.340
